"25721094"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE63nnn/GSE63545/","geo2r":"yes","bioproject":"PRJNA268181"},"200058162":{"uid":"200058162","accession":"GSE58162","gds":"","title":"Analysis of gene expression to find the effect of aspirin on oral cancer cell line","summary":"Aspirin is a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug. Till date there is no information on the molecular mechanism of aspirin on oral cancer cells. In this study, treated oral cancer cells were compared with untreated ones for gene expression for finding the effect of aspirin on biological process and significant pathways involved. Aspirin plays an important role in inducing apoptotic effect by activating regulators and further inhibits cell cycle progression.","gpl":"10904","gse":"58162","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by array","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2014/11/22","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM1402562","title":"Aspirin treated rep 1 on chip1"},{"accession":"GSM1402559","title":"Control rep 1 on chip1"},{"accession":"GSM1402564","title":"Aspirin treated rep 3 on chip1"},{"accession":"GSM1402561","title":"Control rep 3 on chip1"},{"accession":"GSM1402563","title":"Aspirin treated rep 2 on chip2"},{"accession":"GSM1402560","title":"Control rep 2 on chip2"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":6,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":[],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE58nnn/GSE58162/","geo2r":"yes","bioproject":"PRJNA251519"},"200051456":{"uid":"200051456","accession":"GSE51456","gds":"","title":"Gene expression in HNSCC cell lines after knockdown of CTTN","summary":"The gene expression level of CTTN was decreased in HPV-negative HNSCC cell line with an amplification and overexpression of CTTN by performing knockdown experiments using RNA interference. Gene expression profiling and consecutive pathway analyses showed a number of deregulated genes known to be involved in metastatic processes such as migration and invasion. Furthermore, three potential downstream targets of CTTN (MAF, MAFB and PLAC2) were identified.","gpl":"6480","gse":"51456","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by array","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2014/10/18","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM1246027","title":"HNO223 stable knockdown CTTN clone 1 rep 2 vs. HNO223 control clone 1 rep 2"},{"accession":"GSM1246024","title":"HNO223 stable knockdown CTTN clone 1 rep 1 vs. HNO223 control clone 2 rep 1"},{"accession":"GSM1246030","title":"HNO223 stable knockdown CTTN clone 2 rep 2 vs. HNO223 control clone 2 rep 2"},{"accession":"GSM1246025","title":"HNO223 stable knockdown CTTN clone 2 rep 1 vs. HNO223 control clone 1 rep 1"},{"accession":"GSM1246028","title":"HNO223 stable knockdown CTTN clone 1 rep 2 vs. HNO223 control clone 2 rep 2"},{"accession":"GSM1246026","title":"HNO223 stable knockdown CTTN clone 2 rep 1 vs. HNO223 control clone 2 rep 1"},{"accession":"GSM1246023","title":"HNO223 stable knockdown CTTN clone 1 rep 1 vs. HNO223 control clone 1 rep 1"},{"accession":"GSM1246029","title":"HNO223 stable knockdown CTTN clone 2 rep 2 vs. HNO223 control clone 1 rep 2"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":8,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":[],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE51nnn/GSE51456/","geo2r":"yes","bioproject":"PRJNA223233"},"200062061":{"uid":"200062061","accession":"GSE62061","gds":"","title":"Genome-wide gene expression analysis of EGFR inhibitor erlotinib-resistant and -sensitive head and neck squamous cell carcinoma cell lines Cal-27, SCC-25, FaDu, and SQ20B","summary":"Despite the role of epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) signaling in head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC) development and progression, clinical trials involving EGFR tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKIs) have yielded poor results in HNSCC patients. Mechanisms of acquired resistance to the EGFR TKI erlotinib was investigated by developing erlotinib-resistant HNSCC cell lines (Cal-27, SCC-25, FaDu, and SQ20B) and comparing their gene expression profiles with their parental erlotinib-sensitive HNSCC cell lines using microarray analyses. Subsequent pathway and network analyses displayed a significant upregulation in immune response pathways. Role of immune/inflammatory signaling in acquired resistance to erlotinib in HNSCC was investigated.","gpl":"10558","gse":"62061","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by array","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2014/10/07","suppfile":"IDAT, TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM1519076","title":"Cal-27-sensitive 0.01% dmso 48 hr-replicate 3"},{"accession":"GSM1524317","title":"SQ20B-sensitive 0.01% dmso 48 hr-replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM1519073","title":"SCC-25-resistant 0.01% dmso 48hr replicate 3"},{"accession":"GSM1524314","title":"FaDu-resistant 0.01% dmso 48hr replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM1519070","title":"SCC-25-sensitive 0.01% dmso 48 hr-replicate 3"},{"accession":"GSM1524320","title":"SQ20B-resistant 0.01% dmso 48hr replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM1519079","title":"Cal-27-resistant 0.01% dmso 48hr replicate 3"},{"accession":"GSM1519075","title":"Cal-27-sensitive 0.01% dmso 48 hr-replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM1524319","title":"SQ20B-resistant 0.01% dmso 48hr replicate 1"},{"accession":"GSM1519078","title":"Cal-27-resistant 0.01% dmso 48hr replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM1524311","title":"FaDu-sensitive 0.01% dmso 48 hr-replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM1524310","title":"FaDu-sensitive 0.01% dmso 48 hr-replicate 1"},{"accession":"GSM1524316","title":"SQ20B-sensitive 0.01% dmso 48 hr-replicate 1"},{"accession":"GSM1519072","title":"SCC-25-resistant 0.01% dmso 48hr replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM1